<MainLayout>

<section id="background" class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <h1>About</h1>
        <p>
            I am an undergraduate student in Astronomical and Planetary Science with a concentration in Astrophysics at Arizona State University. My academic interests include observational astronomy, planetary science, scientific computing, and astronomical instrumentation. I created this website to document my academic development through independent projects, observing, scientific software, and future research experiences that will shape my academic career.
        </p>
        <p>
            Before returning to university to study astronomy, I earned a bachelor's degree in Information Technology and spent more than six years as a professional frontend software engineer. During that time, astronomy remained a constant part of my life through observational astronomy, astronomical imaging, and public outreach. As my involvement in astronomy grew, I realized I wanted to contribute directly to astronomical research rather than participate solely as a hobbyist. Returning to university was a deliberate decision to pursue astronomical research and, ultimately, graduate study.
        </p>
        <p>
           I am particularly interested in understanding the surfaces and evolution of planetary bodies through observational techniques and image analysis. My background in software engineering has also led to an interest in scientific computing, and I enjoy building software that makes astronomical data easier to analyze, visualize, and explore. During my undergraduate studies, I hope to combine computational methods with observational research while contributing to projects in planetary science or astrophysics. As my experience grows, I intend for this website to evolve alongside it, documenting research, observational work, scientific software, outreach, and other milestones throughout my academic career.
        </p>
        
        
        <h2> Education </h2>
        <h3> Arizona State University </h3>
        <p> 
            B.S. in Astronomical and Planetary Science<br>
            Concentration in Astrophysics<br>
            Expected Graduation: Fall 2028
        </p>
    
        <h3> Kennesaw State University </h3>
        <p> 
            Bachelor of Science in Information Technology, with a concentration in mobile and web development, providing a foundation in software engineering, web development, and computing.
        </p>
                
        <h2> Professional Experience</h2>
        <h3>Astronomical League</h3>
        <p>
            Serves as Assistant Webmaster for the Astronomical League, supporting the organization's website and digital communications.
        </p>
    
        <h3> Software Engineering </h3>
        <p> 
            More than six years of professional experience as a lead frontend software engineer, designing and developing web applications and user interfaces. This background now informs my interest in scientific computing and astronomy software.
        </p>

        <h2> Astronomy &amp; Outreach </h2>
        <h3> Observational Astronomy </h3>
        <p> 
            More than six years of experience in observational astronomy, including solar, lunar, planetary, and deep-sky observing and imaging. My observational work has involved a variety of telescopes, astronomical cameras, and related instrumentation, along with participation in Astronomical League observing programs.
        </p>
        <h3> Science Communication </h3>
        <p> 
            In addition to observing, I enjoy communicating astronomy to public audiences through presentations and STEM outreach. I have presented four public astronomy talks and participated in outreach events for schools and community organizations, contributing more than 60 hours of volunteer outreach.
        </p>
